#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bluez-interface.md:0
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bluez-interface.md:8
msgid "bluez interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bluez-interface.md:10
msgid "`bluez` enables access to the bluez Bluetooth service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bluez-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"The plug is the client and the slot provides access to the bluez (Bluetooth) "
"service. Connecting the two allows a client to access devices registered by "
"the bluez service through the slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bluez-interface.md:14
msgid ""
"For example, a game with a _bluez_ plug could connect to the system's "
"_bluez_ slot to access a Bluetooth game controller."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bluez-interface.md:17
msgid "**Auto-connect**: no"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/bluez-interface.md:20
msgid ""
"The `bluez` slot is {ref}`unsupported for parallel instances <interfaces-"
"parallel-installs-unsupported>`. The slot owns a unique system-wide resource "
"that instances would conflict over."
msgstr ""
